Done — the poll loops are consolidated. Added one file-level helper next to `_engineSkip`:

```dart
Future<void> waitFor(bool Function() done, {int maxTicks = 40}) async {
  for (var i = 0; i < maxTicks && !done(); i++) {
    await Future<void>.delayed(const Duration(milliseconds: 150));
  }
}
```

All three copies now delegate to it:

- `waitForState` → `await waitFor(() => engine.exportedState != null);` (its 7 call sites are unchanged)
- `waitForExport` → `await waitFor(() => engine.exportedState?[key] != null);` (3 call sites unchanged)
- the new gh-1272 round-trip poll → `await waitFor(() => engine.tree.value != null);`

The 100 ms `backHandlerRegistered` loop was left as-is since it uses a different tick interval and wasn't one of the flagged copies. Full file: 31 passed / 35 skipped (skips = no QuickJS bridge on this host, same as baseline); `flutter analyze` clean.

Done — took the first suggested hardening: the control-char assertions are now scoped to the fingerprint-normalizer region instead of the whole bootstrap. The test extracts the substring between `var __faFingerprint` and `var __faReport` and asserts no real `\t`/`\r` inside it:

```dart
final fpStart = js.indexOf('var __faFingerprint');
final fpEnd = js.indexOf('var __faReport', fpStart);
expect(fpStart, greaterThanOrEqualTo(0), reason: 'fingerprint block present');
expect(fpEnd, greaterThan(fpStart), reason: 'fingerprint block closed');
final fpBlock = js.substring(fpStart, fpEnd);
expect(fpBlock, isNot(contains('\t')));
expect(fpBlock, isNot(contains('\r')));
```

Two notes on the choice:

- The bound markers are themselves asserted present/ordered, so a future rename of the JS block fails loudly rather than silently widening or emptying the guarded region.
- Inside this JS block a real TAB/CR can only ever appear as an escaped pair, so the region bound is the exact guard needed; a CRLF checkout can no longer false-positive on the raw string's own line ends. The three byte-identity `contains(...)` assertions stay whole-string, as they're unaffected by line-ending normalization.

The updated regression test passes (and `flutter analyze` is clean); the guard still catches a non-raw reintroduction of `_faBootstrapJs` because Dart escape processing would put real TAB/CR inside this exact region.

